#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM percuma tentang maklumat dan pengkomputeran kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Approach to fault tolerance"
msgstr "Pendekatan kepada toleransi ralat"

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "An approach to fault tolerance {#an-approach-to-fault-tolerance}"
msgstr "Pendekatan kepada toleransi ralat {#an-approach-to-fault-tolerance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll begin by outlining a basic approach to fault-tolerant quantum "
"computing based on quantum circuits and error correcting codes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan mulakan dengan menggariskan pendekatan asas kepada pengkomputeran "
"kuantum toleran ralat berdasarkan litar kuantum dan kod pembetulan ralat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the sake of this discussion, let us consider the following example of a quantum circuit.\n"
"This happens to be a teleportation circuit, including the preparation of the e-bit, but the specific functionality of the circuit is immaterial — it's just an example, and in actuality we're likely to be interested in significantly larger circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk tujuan perbincangan ini, mari kita pertimbangkan contoh litar kuantum berikut.\n"
"Ini kebetulan merupakan litar teleportasi, termasuk penyediaan e-bit, tetapi fungsi spesifik litar ini tidak penting — ini hanyalah sebuah contoh, dan sebenarnya kita mungkin lebih berminat dengan litar yang jauh lebih besar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A teleportation circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-"
"error-correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/teleportation-"
"circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A teleportation circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-"
"error-correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/teleportation-"
"circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A circuit like this one represents an ideal, and an actual implementation of it won't be perfect.\n"
"So what could go wrong?\n"
msgstr ""
"Litar seperti ini mewakili sesuatu yang ideal, dan pelaksanaan sebenarnya tidak akan sempurna.\n"
"Jadi apa yang boleh berlaku salah?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fact of the matter is that quite a lot could go wrong!\n"
"In particular, the state initializations, unitary operations, and measurements will all be imperfect;\n"
"and the qubits themselves will be susceptible to noise, including decoherence, at every point in the computation, even when no operations are being performed on them and they're simply storing quantum information.\n"
"That is to say, just about everything could go wrong.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hakikatnya adalah bahawa banyak perkara boleh berlaku salah!\n"
"Khususnya, permulaan keadaan, operasi unitari, dan pengukuran semuanya tidak sempurna;\n"
"dan qubit itu sendiri akan terdedah kepada hingar, termasuk penyahkoheranan, pada setiap titik dalam pengiraan, walaupun ketika tiada operasi sedang dilakukan ke atasnya dan ia hanya menyimpan maklumat kuantum.\n"
"Maksudnya, hampir segala-galanya boleh berlaku salah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is one exception, though: Any *classical* computations that are involved are assumed to be perfect — because, practically speaking, classical computations are perfect.\n"
"For example, if we decide to use a surface code for error correction, and a classical perfect matching algorithm is run to compute corrections, we really don't need to concern ourselves with the possibility that errors in this classical computation will lead to a faulty solution.\n"
"As another example, quantum computations often necessitate classical pre- and post-processing, and these classical computations can safely be assumed to be perfect as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun ada satu pengecualian: Sebarang pengiraan *klasik* yang terlibat dianggap sempurna — kerana, secara praktisnya, pengiraan klasik memang sempurna.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, jika kita memutuskan untuk menggunakan kod permukaan untuk pembetulan ralat, dan algoritma padanan sempurna klasik dijalankan untuk mengira pembetulan, kita sebenarnya tidak perlu bimbang tentang kemungkinan ralat dalam pengiraan klasik ini akan menghasilkan penyelesaian yang salah.\n"
"Sebagai contoh lain, pengiraan kuantum sering memerlukan pemprosesan awal dan akhir secara klasik, dan pengiraan klasik ini juga boleh dianggap sempurna dengan selamat.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Noise models {#noise-models}"
msgstr "Model hingar {#noise-models}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze fault-tolerant implementations of quantum circuits, we require a precise mathematical model — a *noise model* — through which *probabilities* for various things to go wrong can be associated.\n"
"Hypothetically speaking, one could attempt to come up with a highly detailed, complicated noise model that aims to reflect the reality of what happens in a particular device.\n"
"But, if the noise model is too complicated or difficult to reason about, it will likely be of limited use.\n"
"For this reason, simpler noise models are much more typically considered.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menganalisis pelaksanaan toleran ralat bagi litar kuantum, kita memerlukan model matematik yang tepat — sebuah *model hingar* — melaluinya *kebarangkalian* pelbagai perkara yang boleh berlaku salah boleh dikaitkan.\n"
"Secara hipotesis, seseorang boleh cuba membuat model hingar yang sangat terperinci dan rumit yang bertujuan untuk mencerminkan realiti apa yang berlaku dalam peranti tertentu.\n"
"Tetapi, jika model hingar terlalu rumit atau susah untuk difikirkan, ia mungkin hanya berguna secara terhad.\n"
"Atas sebab ini, model hingar yang lebih mudah biasanya lebih banyak dipertimbangkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One example of a simple noise model is the *independent stochastic noise model*, where errors or faults affecting different components at different moments in time — or, in other words, different *locations* in a quantum circuit — are assumed to be independent.\n"
"For instance, each gate might fail with a certain probability, an error might strike each stored qubit per unit time\n"
"with a different probability, and so on, with *no correlations* among the different possible errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu contoh model hingar yang mudah ialah *model hingar stokastik bebas*, di mana ralat atau kerosakan yang mempengaruhi komponen berbeza pada masa berbeza — atau, dalam erti kata lain, *lokasi* berbeza dalam litar kuantum — dianggap bebas.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, setiap gate mungkin gagal dengan kebarangkalian tertentu, ralat mungkin menyerang setiap qubit yang tersimpan per unit masa\n"
"dengan kebarangkalian yang berbeza, dan sebagainya, dengan *tiada korelasi* di antara pelbagai ralat yang mungkin berlaku.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, it is certainly reasonable to object to such a model, because there probably will be correlations among errors in real physical devices.\n"
"For instance, there might be a small chance of a catastrophic error that wipes out all the qubits at once.\n"
"Perhaps more likely, there could be errors that are localized but that nevertheless affect multiple components in a quantum computer.\n"
"Nobody suggests otherwise!\n"
"Nevertheless, the independent stochastic noise model does provide a simple baseline that captures the idea that nature is unpredictable but not malicious, and it isn't intentionally trying to ruin quantum computations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memang wajar untuk membantah model sedemikian, kerana mungkin ada korelasi di antara ralat dalam peranti fizikal sebenar.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, mungkin ada peluang kecil ralat bencana yang menghapuskan semua qubit sekaligus.\n"
"Mungkin lebih mungkin, ada ralat yang terlokalisasi tetapi tetap mempengaruhi pelbagai komponen dalam komputer kuantum.\n"
"Tidak ada yang mencadangkan sebaliknya!\n"
"Namun begitu, model hingar stokastik bebas memberikan asas mudah yang menangkap idea bahawa alam semula jadi tidak dapat diramal tetapi tidak berniat jahat, dan ia tidak dengan sengaja cuba merosakkan pengiraan kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Other, less forgiving noise models are also commonly studied.\n"
"For example, a common relaxation of the assumption of independence among errors affecting different locations in a quantum circuit is that *just the locations* of the errors are independent, but the actual errors affecting these locations could be correlated.\n"
msgstr ""
"Model hingar lain yang kurang bertolak ansur juga biasa dikaji.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, kelonggaran umum daripada andaian kebebasan di antara ralat yang mempengaruhi lokasi berbeza dalam litar kuantum ialah *hanya lokasi* ralat yang bebas, tetapi ralat sebenar yang mempengaruhi lokasi ini boleh berkorelasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Regardless of what noise model is chosen, it should be recognized that "
"*learning* about the errors that affect specific devices, and formulating "
"new error models if the old ones lead us astray, could potentially be an "
"important part of the development of fault-tolerant quantum computation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tanpa mengira model hingar yang dipilih, perlu diakui bahawa *mempelajari* "
"tentang ralat yang mempengaruhi peranti tertentu, dan merumuskan model ralat"
" baru jika yang lama menjerumuskan kita, berpotensi menjadi bahagian penting"
" dalam pembangunan pengiraan kuantum toleran ralat.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fault-tolerant circuit implementations {#fault-tolerant-circuit-"
"implementations}"
msgstr ""
"Pelaksanaan litar toleran ralat {#fault-tolerant-circuit-implementations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we'll consider a basic strategy for fault-tolerant implementations of quantum circuits.\n"
"We'll use the teleportation circuit above as a running example to illustrate the strategy, though it could be applied to any quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya kita akan mempertimbangkan strategi asas untuk pelaksanaan toleran ralat bagi litar kuantum.\n"
"Kita akan menggunakan litar teleportasi di atas sebagai contoh berterusan untuk menggambarkan strategi ini, walaupun ia boleh diterapkan pada mana-mana litar kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a diagram of a fault-tolerant implementation of our teleportation "
"circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah gambar rajah pelaksanaan toleran ralat bagi litar teleportasi"
" kita.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fault-tolerant implementation of a teleportation "
"circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/FT-teleportation-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fault-tolerant implementation of a teleportation "
"circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/FT-teleportation-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The individual components in this diagram and their connection to the "
"original circuit are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Komponen individu dalam gambar rajah ini dan hubungannya dengan litar asal "
"adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"State preparations, unitary gates, and measurements are not performed "
"directly, as single operations, but rather are performed by so-called "
"*gadgets*, which could each involve multiple qubits and multiple operations."
" In the diagram, gadgets are indicated by purple boxes labelled by whatever "
"state preparation, gate, or measurement is to be implemented.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penyediaan keadaan, gate unitari, dan pengukuran tidak dilakukan secara "
"langsung, sebagai operasi tunggal, tetapi sebaliknya dilakukan oleh apa yang"
" dipanggil *gadget*, yang masing-masing boleh melibatkan pelbagai qubit dan "
"pelbagai operasi. Dalam gambar rajah, gadget ditunjukkan dengan kotak ungu "
"berlabel dengan apa jua penyediaan keadaan, gate, atau pengukuran yang "
"hendak dilaksanakan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *logical* qubits on which the original, ideal circuit is run are "
"protected using a quantum error correcting code. Rather than acting directly"
" on these logical qubits, the gadgets act on the *physical* qubits that "
"encode them. The diagram suggests that five physical qubits are used for "
"each logical qubit, as if the $5$-qubit code were being used, but the number"
" could naturally be different. It is worth stressing that these logical "
"qubits are *never* exposed; they spend their entire existence being "
"protected by whatever quantum error correcting code we've chosen.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qubit *logik* di mana litar asal yang ideal dijalankan dilindungi "
"menggunakan kod pembetulan ralat kuantum. Daripada bertindak secara langsung"
" ke atas qubit logik ini, gadget bertindak ke atas qubit *fizikal* yang "
"mengekodnya. Gambar rajah menunjukkan bahawa lima qubit fizikal digunakan "
"untuk setiap qubit logik, seolah-olah kod $5$-Qubit sedang digunakan, tetapi"
" jumlahnya boleh berbeza secara semula jadi. Perlu ditekankan bahawa qubit "
"logik ini *tidak pernah* didedahkan; ia menghabiskan seluruh kewujudannya "
"dilindungi oleh kod pembetulan ralat kuantum yang kita pilih.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Error correction is performed repeatedly, as suggested by the blue boxes "
"labeled \"EC\" in the diagram, throughout the computation. It is critically "
"important that this is done both frequently and in parallel. As errors take "
"place, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Entropy is a measure of randomness, "
"uncertainty, or disorder in a system.\">entropy</DefinitionTooltip> builds "
"up, and constant work is required to remove it from the system at a high "
"enough rate to allow the computation to function correctly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pembetulan ralat dilakukan berulang kali, seperti yang disarankan oleh kotak"
" biru berlabel \"EC\" dalam gambar rajah, sepanjang pengiraan. Adalah sangat"
" penting bahawa ini dilakukan dengan kerap dan secara selari. Apabila ralat "
"berlaku, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Entropi adalah ukuran rawaknya, "
"ketidakpastian, atau huru-hara dalam sesuatu "
"sistem.\">entropi</DefinitionTooltip> terbina, dan kerja berterusan "
"diperlukan untuk membuangnya dari sistem pada kadar yang cukup tinggi agar "
"pengiraan berfungsi dengan betul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are therefore specific choices that must be made, including the selection of the gadgets as well as the quantum error correcting code itself.\n"
"Once these choices have been made, and assuming a particular noise model has been adopted, there is a fundamental question that we may ask ourselves:\n"
"Is this actually helping?\n"
"That is, are we making things better, or might we actually be making things worse?\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh itu ada pilihan spesifik yang mesti dibuat, termasuk pemilihan gadget serta kod pembetulan ralat kuantum itu sendiri.\n"
"Setelah pilihan-pilihan ini dibuat, dan dengan mengandaikan model hingar tertentu telah diterima pakai, ada soalan asas yang boleh kita tanyakan kepada diri sendiri:\n"
"Adakah ini sebenarnya membantu?\n"
"Iaitu, adakah kita menjadikan perkara lebih baik, atau mungkin kita sebenarnya menjadikan perkara lebih buruk?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the rate of noise is too high, the entire process just suggested could very well be making things worse, just like the 9-qubit Shor code makes things worse for independent errors if the error probability on each qubit is above the break-even point.\n"
"If, however, the rate of noise is below a certain threshold, then all of this extra work will get us somewhere — and as we'll discuss toward the end of the lesson, paths open up for further error reduction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kadar hingar terlalu tinggi, keseluruhan proses yang baru dicadangkan ini boleh menjadikan perkara lebih buruk, sama seperti kod Shor 9-Qubit menjadikan perkara lebih buruk untuk ralat bebas jika kebarangkalian ralat pada setiap qubit melebihi titik impas.\n"
"Namun, jika kadar hingar berada di bawah ambang tertentu, maka semua kerja tambahan ini akan membawa kita ke suatu tempat — dan seperti yang akan kita bincangkan menjelang akhir pelajaran, jalan terbuka untuk pengurangan ralat selanjutnya.\n"
